--TEST--
`SecretEntry::of`'s lifetime is a `Core\Time\Duration`, and a count of seconds is not one — `rule:core-api/shape-rules`, `rule:core-api/units-are-types`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// R12: the unit is the type. A member taking an `int` would have to pick a
// scale and document it, and every call site would have to remember which one
// it picked — so `30` is refused where `30s` is the whole of what a lifetime
// is written as. It is also what makes the entry's own slot compiled code's
// business rather than a program's: nothing but a `Duration` reaches it.
var $entry = Core\Cache\SecretEntry::of("token", 30);
echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `Core\Time\Duration`, found `int`
  --> case.nvs:7:50
%A
